<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Fencing in Carrollton usually starts with an older wood fence on a lot built between the 1970s and the 1990s. The city sits north-northwest of Dallas and spreads across Dallas, Denton and Collin counties, and many of its subdivisions have alley-backed lots where the rear fence or gate faces the alley. This site is advertising for independent fence contractors and does not build or repair anything itself.</p><p>Call (214) 555-0137 and describe the job: a leaning fence, storm damage, a gate that will not open or a new fence. An independent contractor quotes the work, and the honest advice is to collect two or three comparable written quotes before you pick one. Carrollton has its own fence rules, so the sections below cover the City's permit trigger, height limits and what to ask before you sign.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Carrollton</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Carrollton Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wood privacy fence installation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A new cedar or pine privacy fence along an older Carrollton lot, including board-on-board styles. The contractor who quotes your job should show how the plan fits the City's 8-ft rear and side limit and your HOA's rules.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Fence repair and storm damage</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Leaning sections, rotted posts and missing pickets are common on 15 to 20 year old fences. Ask whether the repair stays under the 20 ft the City treats as the permit line.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Gate repair and automatic gates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Sagging walk gates, failed latches and driveway openers that quit. Power wiring for an opener is electrical work, so ask the installer who holds the electrical licence.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3DFD8;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A3035;margin:0 0 8px;">Wrought iron and ornamental fences</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tubular steel or aluminum fencing for a front yard or side run. The City limits a Carrollton front-yard fence to 36 inches and no more than 50 percent opacity, which suits open iron.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
